{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#743","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#743","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#743\",\"parent_revision\":\"f6adf524ba93d9fea07f9066e6375029180471a028962e77a8f950012aeb589c\",\"root_revision\":\"f6adf524ba93d9fea07f9066e6375029180471a028962e77a8f950012aeb589c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe grooming process produces an Impact Radius section listing every file affected by a change. The planning process (swarm-task-planner + plan-validator) creates tasks and validates acceptance criteria coverage. But nothing verifies that every Impact Radius item either has a task covering it or an explicit documented reason for exclusion.\\n\\nObserved on #719: Impact Radius identified 72 affected files. The swarm-task-planner created 14 tasks covering only the 7 primary components. 39 files had no task \u2014 including the code-reviewer agent (a task file producer), 6 backlog_core consumers, 16 agent instruction files, and 8 documentation files. The plan-validator checked that acceptance criteria mapped to tasks, but the acceptance criteria only listed the 7 primary components \u2014 the Impact Radius was not checked.\\n\\nThe gap is between grooming (which discovers affected systems) and planning (which creates tasks). The Ecosystem Completeness Checklist at the bottom of every Impact Radius section is never verified against the task plan.\\n\\nWhat success looks like: the plan-validator agent checks that every Impact Radius item in the groomed backlog item either (a) has a task in the plan, (b) is covered by a task that handles its category (e.g., T14 \\\"sync development-harness\\\" covers all harness agent copies), or (c) has an explicit exclusion note in the plan explaining why no task is needed. Items classified as MAYBE in the Impact Radius get a verification task to confirm whether they need changes.\\n\\nHow you'll know it's working: plan validation on a plan like #719 would report \\\"39 Impact Radius items have no covering task \u2014 BLOCKED until tasks or exclusions are added.\\\"\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-05-24\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `plan-validator` agent exists with Dimension 10 (Impact Radius Coverage) | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md` lines 407-462 |\\n| 2 | Dimension 10 is already implemented with blocker/warning severity rules, direct/category/exclusion-note checks | AVAILABLE | plan-validator.md lines 422-461 |\\n| 3 | `swarm-task-planner` agent has no Impact Radius mention or IR coverage guidance | AVAILABLE (gap confirmed) | `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 zero matches for 'Impact Radius' |\\n| 4 | `groom-backlog-item` skill does not document the `<!-- IR-EXCLUDE: {file} \u2014 {reason} -->` exclusion note format | MISSING | `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/` \u2014 no IR-EXCLUDE string found in any reference file |\\n| 5 | `task-decomposition` skill has no IR coverage guidance | AVAILABLE (gap confirmed) | `plugins/development-harness/skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md` \u2014 zero matches for 'Impact Radius' |\\n| 6 | #719 plan available as regression reference case | DERIVABLE | `backlog_view(selector='#719', section='Impact Radius')` \u2014 72 files identified, 14 tasks covering 7 components, 39 uncovered |\\n| 7 | Exclusion note format (`<!-- IR-EXCLUDE: {file} \u2014 {reason} -->`) not yet standardized in any skill or agent file | MISSING | grep over all skills and agents \u2014 zero matches for 'IR-EXCLUDE' |\\n\\nVerdict: **APPROVED-WITH-GAPS** \u2014 plan-validator Dimension 10 already exists and is fully implemented. Gaps are: (1) swarm-task-planner agent has no IR guidance so planners are never prompted to cover IR entries; (2) groom-backlog-item documents no exclusion note format so plan authors have no standard way to document intentional exclusions; (3) task-decomposition skill has no IR cross-reference.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 P1 Bug. Every plan produced by the swarm-task-planner can silently miss affected files that the groomer identified. The validation gap is systemic: plan-validator Dimension 10 is fully implemented (lines 407-462) but swarm-task-planner produces no IR coverage tasks and groom-backlog-item documents no exclusion format, so Dimension 10 silently passes by default when no IR is addressed. Observed on #719: 39 of 72 Impact Radius files had no covering task.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: any implementation plan where groomed Impact Radius lists files not covered by tasks \u2014 the omission is undetected until post-implementation discovery\\n- Bottleneck: plan-validator Dimension 10 is wired but silently skips when no backlog item reference is provided \u2014 swarm-task-planner does not pass one and does not guide planners to produce IR-covering tasks\\n- Affects: every feature implementation that goes through the dh pipeline and has a groomed backlog item with an Impact Radius section\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Every plan is validated against its Impact Radius before execution \u2014 no silent file omissions\\n- Planners receive explicit guidance to cover or exclude IR entries when decomposing tasks\\n- Exclusion format gives plan authors a structured, standard way to document intentional scope decisions\\n- Regression: plan-validator on #719 would report '39 Impact Radius items have no covering task \u2014 BLOCKED'\\n- Future groomers produce IR sections with higher confidence that downstream planning will honour them\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a plan references a backlog item (via `issue` frontmatter field), plan-validator reads the Impact Radius section from that item and checks every listed file or system against the task plan. If any MUST/unqualified IR entry has no covering task and no `<!-- IR-EXCLUDE: {file} \u2014 {reason} -->` note, validation returns BLOCKED with a structured list of uncovered items under the `impact_radius_coverage` dimension. MAYBE-classified entries with no verification task and no exclusion note return as warnings. Plans with no backlog item reference record Dimension 10 as `skipped` \u2014 not a blocker.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `plan-validator` Dimension 10 is exercised whenever a plan has a backlog item reference \u2014 observable: running plan-validator on a plan that references a backlog item with an Impact Radius section produces either 'impact radius coverage: pass' or a BLOCKED result listing uncovered entries\\n- `swarm-task-planner` agent file includes explicit IR coverage guidance so task decompositions address each IR category \u2014 observable: plans produced for items with IR sections contain tasks or exclusion notes for every IR entry\\n- `groom-backlog-item` skill reference files document the `<!-- IR-EXCLUDE: {file} \u2014 {reason} -->` exclusion note format \u2014 observable: the format string appears in `skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` or `SKILL.md`\\n- No plan passes Dimension 10 with uncovered MUST/unqualified IR entries when the plan has a backlog item reference\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `plan-validator` reads the Impact Radius section from the groomed backlog item when the plan's `issue` frontmatter field contains a backlog item selector\\n2. For each Impact Radius entry, validator checks: (a) a task explicitly names the file/path, (b) a task explicitly states it covers the entry's category, or (c) an `<!-- IR-EXCLUDE: {file} \u2014 {reason} -->` exclusion note appears in the plan\\n3. If any MUST/unqualified IR entry has no covering task and no exclusion note: validator returns BLOCKED with a structured list of uncovered items under the `impact_radius_coverage` dimension\\n4. MAYBE-classified IR entries with no verification task and no exclusion note return as warnings, not blockers\\n5. If the plan has no `issue` field or the referenced item has no Impact Radius section, Dimension 10 records as `skipped` or `n/a` \u2014 not a blocker\\n6. `swarm-task-planner` agent file contains explicit guidance to address Impact Radius items when decomposing tasks \u2014 observable: the word 'Impact Radius' appears in the agent file\\n7. `groom-backlog-item` skill reference files document the `<!-- IR-EXCLUDE: {file} \u2014 {reason} -->` exclusion note format \u2014 observable: `IR-EXCLUDE` appears in at least one file under `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/`\\n8. Regression check: plan-validator run against the plan for #719 reports 39 Impact Radius items as uncovered (BLOCKED)\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Agent | `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md` \u2014 Dimension 10 lines 407-462 (already implemented) |\\n| Agent | `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 task decomposition section to extend with IR guidance |\\n| Skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` \u2014 Impact Radius output format at line 106; exclusion format to be added |\\n| Skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md` \u2014 Impact Radius required section rule at line 18 |\\n| Skill | `plugins/development-harness/skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md` \u2014 task decomposition skill (no IR guidance currently) |\\n| Prior work | plan-validator.md lines 70-169 \u2014 Drafting State Handling; Dimension 10 deferred until finalize (line 110) |\\n| Regression | GitHub Issue #719 \u2014 72 Impact Radius files identified in groomed item; 14 tasks covering 7 components; 39 uncovered |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 plan-validator Dimension 10 is already fully implemented; changes are guidance and documentation additions only\\n- Blocks: any implementation plan quality gate that relies on Impact Radius coverage enforcement\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 plan-validator Dimension 10 is fully implemented (lines 407-462 verified). Work is limited to: (1) verifying the end-to-end wiring (plan `issue` field \u2192 `backlog_view` \u2192 Dimension 10 check \u2014 likely already wired per lines 414-416), (2) adding IR guidance text to `swarm-task-planner` agent, (3) documenting `IR-EXCLUDE` exclusion format in `groom-backlog-item` skill references, (4) optionally cross-referencing from `task-decomposition` skill. No algorithmic changes to plan-validator required.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md` \u2014 add Impact Radius coverage check to validation steps\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/` \u2014 document exclusion note format in grooming guidelines\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/swarm-task-planner/` \u2014 add IR coverage guidance to task decomposition\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n**Code Producers (MUST):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md` \u2014 Dimension 10 already implemented (lines 407-462); verify end-to-end wiring: plan `issue` field \u2192 `backlog_view` call \u2192 IR extraction \u2192 coverage check\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 add explicit IR coverage guidance to task decomposition section; currently zero mentions of Impact Radius\\n\\n**Documentation (MUST):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` \u2014 add exclusion note format documentation (`<!-- IR-EXCLUDE: {file} \u2014 {reason} -->`); currently documents IR output format but not exclusion notes\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 reference exclusion format so plan authors know the standard\\n\\n**Agent Instructions (MAYBE):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md` \u2014 may need IR coverage guidance cross-referenced; currently zero matches for 'Impact Radius'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/planning/` \u2014 may reference plan-validator Dimension 10 for completeness\\n\\n**Ecosystem Completeness Checklist:**\\n- [ ] plan-validator Dimension 10 wiring verified end-to-end (issue field \u2192 backlog_view \u2192 IR check)\\n- [ ] swarm-task-planner updated with IR coverage guidance\\n- [ ] groom-backlog-item exclusion format documented (IR-EXCLUDE)\\n- [ ] task-decomposition skill cross-reference added (if applicable)\\n- [ ] Regression test: plan-validator on #719 plan returns BLOCKED with 39 uncovered IR items\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a plan-validator agent, I need to verify that every file in the Impact Radius section either has a covering task in the plan or an explicit documented exclusion so that no affected file silently escapes implementation coverage.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **impact radius findings must become plan tasks or documented exclusions \u2014 39 of 72 files had no task in #719** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 39 of 72 Impact Radius files had no task in #719 plan (2026-03-15)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b217346576d0b39bf87aa0bb71c14b6b23e093f3be4e940e7112eaf7f79b230e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTEH2Q\"}"}